WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.230
<v Mishu>Here's a challenge. Five friends will measure this table with their handspans.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.952
<v Mishu>Will they all get the same answer?

00:00:07.952 --> 00:00:10.086
<v Rohan>Of course! It's the same table.

00:00:10.086 --> 00:00:12.393
<v Ishita>I'm not so sure. Let's see.

00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:17.596
<v Mishu>Look! Five friends, one table. Thirteen handspans. A little more than thirteen.

00:00:17.496 --> 00:00:21.347
<v Mishu>A little less. Between thirteen and fourteen. Fourteen!

00:00:21.347 --> 00:00:24.349
<v Rohan>Five different answers? Somebody counted wrong!

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:26.536
<v Mishu>Nobody counted wrong. Look again.

00:00:26.536 --> 00:00:29.373
<v Mishu>The table did not change. The hands did.

00:00:29.273 --> 00:00:36.642
<v Mishu>For thousands of years, people measured with arm length, foot length, paces, handspans and the width of four fingers.

00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:40.031
<v Mishu>And they all had this problem: no two bodies are the same.

00:00:40.031 --> 00:00:42.806
<v Rohan>Wait. What exactly is arm length?

00:00:42.806 --> 00:00:45.039
<v Mishu>Arm length is also called a cubit.

00:00:44.939 --> 00:00:49.099
<v Mishu>It is the distance from your elbow to the tip of your middle finger.

00:00:49.099 --> 00:00:52.433
<v Rohan>Then my cubit is much shorter than my dad's!

00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:54.160
<v Ishita>And what is a yard length?

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:01.019
<v Mishu>A yard length is the distance from your nose to the tips of your fingers, with your arm stretched out.

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:05.189
<v Rohan>Let's try footsteps too! Heel to toe, across the classroom.

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:08.518
<v Mishu>Good idea! Measure your classroom with your footsteps.

00:01:08.418 --> 00:01:12.664
<v Mishu>Then ask four friends to do the same, and compare the five readings.

00:01:12.564 --> 00:01:13.938
<v Mishu>Are they equal?

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:17.264
<v Rohan>No way! Our feet are all different sizes.

00:01:17.264 --> 00:01:20.813
<v Ishita>So we need something that is the same for everyone.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:24.456
<v Mishu>Exactly. Keep that thought. We'll need it on our tour.
